      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e2",
      "title": "Watch out",
      "body": "Before a word that starts with a consonant, six, dix and huit lose their last sound: six livres (see LEEvr), dix livres (dee LEEvr), huit jours (wee ZHOOR). Before a vowel they link: six ans (see-ZAH(N)), dix ans (dee-ZAH(N)), neuf ans (nuh-VAH(N))."
    },
