      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e3",
      "title": "In Canada",
      "body": "In Canada, phone numbers are said in short groups. You will hear cinq-un-quatre for 514 (Montréal), six-un-trois for 613 (Ottawa), quatre-un-six for 416 (Toronto). Postal codes mix letters and digits, so your alphabet from 0.2 is useful here."
    },
